cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use DockAnalyzer in your research, please cite the software using the metadata
  below. DockAnalyzer is not yet formally published, and a DOI is not currently available.
title: 'DockAnalyzer: A modular Python toolkit for protein–ligand interaction analysis in
  UCSF ChimeraX'
type: software
authors:
- family-names: Bastos
  given-names: Leonardo Marensi
abstract: DockAnalyzer is a modular Python toolkit for identifying, classifying, scoring,
  reporting, and visualizing protein–ligand interactions from molecular docking studies in
  UCSF ChimeraX and compatible Python environments.
repository-code: https://github.com/LeonardoMBastos/Binding-contacts-analysis-in-ChimeraX-
url: https://github.com/LeonardoMBastos/Binding-contacts-analysis-in-ChimeraX-
license: MIT
keywords:
- molecular docking
- protein-ligand interactions
- UCSF ChimeraX
- computational chemistry
- structural analysis
- Python
